      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fairhope was founded in 1894 as a single‑tax colony inspired by economist Henry George, one of the few intentional communities of its kind.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/pennsylvania_fairhope",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "This tiny town sits along the historic B&O Railroad, a line that once ferried coal and passengers across Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairhope%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fairhope’s name reflects its founders’ optimism about the future, not a view of rolling hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/pennsylvania_fairhope",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The B&O line through Fairhope still runs today, now operated by CSX Transportation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
